HST Office: controls made in HST get room for their caption in Office.

In real Excel and Word, the text of buttons, check boxes and option buttons on a form made in HST sat low and
was clipped. Such controls name no font; they now get the height a Tahoma 8 caption needs in a bordered box
at 96 and 120 DPI, about 18.7 pt (Office's own default is 18 pt). Controls read from an Office file name the
font they had and keep their size.

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: tests/runtime/check-vba-forms.py.
---
--- a/oox/source/ole/vbaformexport.cxx
+++ b/oox/source/ole/vbaformexport.cxx
@@ -185,11 +185,28 @@
     PropertySet aPropSet(rNode.mxProps);
     xModel->convertFromProperties(aPropSet, rConv);
 
-    // A dialog control usually names no font, and an empty name leaves the choice to Forms, whose fallback
-    // does not fit the control. Office-made forms name Tahoma, which has Vietnamese.
+    // A control made in HST names no font (one read from an Office file keeps the font it had), and an
+    // empty name leaves the choice to Forms, whose fallback does not fit the control. Office-made forms
+    // name Tahoma, which has Vietnamese. Such a control also gets the height a Tahoma 8 caption needs in a
+    // bordered box at 96 and 120 DPI (Office's own default is 18 pt): shorter ones showed the text low and
+    // clipped in real Excel and Word. Forms read from Office files are written with their sizes.
     if (auto* pFont = dynamic_cast<AxFontDataModel*>(xModel.get()))
+    {
         if (pFont->maFontData.maFontName.isEmpty())
+        {
             pFont->maFontData.maFontName = u"Tahoma"_ustr;
+            constexpr sal_Int32 nMinTextHeight = 660; // 1/100 mm, about 18.7 pt
+            switch (rNode.mnClass)
+            {
+                case SITE_COMMANDBUTTON: case SITE_TOGGLEBUTTON: case SITE_CHECKBOX:
+                case SITE_OPTIONBUTTON: case SITE_TEXTBOX: case SITE_COMBOBOX:
+                    rNode.maSize.second = std::max(rNode.maSize.second, nMinTextHeight);
+                    break;
+                default:
+                    break;
+            }
+        }
+    }
 
     if (auto* pMorph = dynamic_cast<AxMorphDataModelBase*>(xModel.get()))
     {
